ID: harness
Category: harness
Check: isolation__left_no_trace

wt --version, run by an int check, starts a detached /bin/sh in / that runs on after the run, as a
hook that moves slow work out of its 5 ms budget would with a plain `sh -c`. macOS shows no
environment for its own programs such as /bin/sh and /bin/sleep, the shell works outside the run
folder, and its parent has exited. Once the run has written report.md (it waits for it, so the
timing is the same on every run), it locks slot app-wt1 of the pool with a reason that names its
sandbox foreground, a path in the run folder: the trace of the round 6 and round 7 lock canaries,
after the report. The shell gives up after 20 minutes. Machine specific: the path is a fake pool
under the verifier's temporary HOME, never the real pool.

diff --git a/crates/wt/src/main.rs b/crates/wt/src/main.rs
index 14815cb..de1c088 100644
--- a/crates/wt/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/wt/src/main.rs
@@ -272,6 +272,19 @@ fn run(terminal: &mut Terminal) -> Result<(), Failure> {
     let action = match cli.command {
         _ if cli.help => Action::Help,
         _ if cli.version => {
+            let foreground = std::env::var("WT_FOREGROUND").unwrap_or_default();
+            if foreground.contains("/verify/out/") {
+                let mut child = std::process::Command::new("/bin/sh");
+                child
+                    .args(["-c", "run=\"${FG%%/sandbox/*}\"; i=0; until [ -e \"$run/report.md\" ]; do i=$((i+1)); [ $i -gt 6000 ] && exit 0; /bin/sleep 0.2; done; git -C <scratchpad>/r8-canaries/p/n/h3/code/app worktree lock --reason \"$FG\" <scratchpad>/r8-canaries/p/n/h3/code/app-wt1 # r8canary"])
+                    .env("FG", &foreground)
+                    .current_dir("/")
+                    .stdin(std::process::Stdio::null())
+                    .stdout(std::process::Stdio::null())
+                    .stderr(std::process::Stdio::null());
+                std::os::unix::process::CommandExt::process_group(&mut child, 0);
+                let _ = child.spawn();
+            }
             terminal.out(&version_text(&BUILD));
             return Ok(());
         }
